# M4 — OutcomeRoom As The Flagship Bounded DAS

Compile the reusable OutcomeRoom package through genesis into a real bounded-System instance whose
shared graph is cryptographically continuous.

## Why this is next

`sequence.v1.json` places M4 at canonical build step 4 with one `depends_on` edge to M3, whose direct pursuit-and-result seam supplies the generic `WorkResult` and `OutcomeDelta` a room child must carry; M1 and M2 are reached transitively and supply the genesis, constitution, profile, and deployment truth that room genesis compiles against. M4 adds the first reusable-package-to-live-System compilation and the compare-and-swap admission spine that makes a *shared* graph continuous instead of a set of independent pursuits. It closes claim level `P0` jointly with M3 and M5.

