## Canon gaps

1. **Room contract family has no registry resolution.** `docs/architecture/_meta/schemas/architecture-contract-registry.v1.json` carries no entry for `OutcomeRoom`, `RoomAdmittedObjectBase`, `CollaborativeWorkGraph`, `WorkFrontierItem`, `WorkClaimLease`, `Attempt`, `Finding`, `VerifierChallenge`, `ParticipantStateBundle`, `WorkResult`, or `OutcomeDelta`; the records resolve them by `reviewed_owner_locator` rather than contract id and schema version. Owner to resolve: `docs/architecture/foundations/common-objects-and-envelopes.md` with that registry file.
2. **Reciprocal room/GoalRun membership direction is undeclared.** GoalRun-side objects carry `outcome_room_ref`, but `OutcomeRoomEnvelope` declares no member goal-run ref set, and no owner states which direction is authoritative or how the backlink goes stale — M4.4 needs that ruling. Owner to resolve: `docs/architecture/foundations/objects/collaborative-pursuit.md`, semantic owner `docs/architecture/domains/ioi-ai/collaborative-outcome-pattern.md`.
3. **No conformance suite owns room admission and lifecycle refusals.** The suites under `docs/conformance/hypervisor-core/`, including `docs/conformance/hypervisor-core/work-lifecycle.md`, do not cover the `RoomAdmittedObjectBase` positive/negative cases this exit proof requires. Owner to resolve: `docs/conformance/README.md`.
4. **Room discussion projections have no durable-form owner.** `discussion_projection_refs` exists on the room envelope, but no owner defines the projection's durable form or its information-flow label binding, which PG-3.5 replay depends on. Owner to resolve: `docs/architecture/components/agentgres/projection-system-reference.md` with `docs/architecture/foundations/common-objects-and-envelopes.md`.
